{"document_id": "b313a966-c2d6-4354-8e9a-e25e97ef0652", "crop": "mango", "organization": "TNAU", "source": "TNAU", "source_url": "https://agritech.tnau.ac.in/crop_protection/crop_prot_postharvest_mango_5.html", "title": "TNAU Agritech Portal :: Crop Protection", "retrieved_at": "2026-09-06T23:41:40.406040", "content": "| ![TNAU Agritech Portal](https://agritech.tnau.ac.in/crop_protection/images/index/cp_index.jpg)  |  \n| --- |  \n|  [Home](https://agritech.tnau.ac.in/index.html \"Home\") | [About Us](https://agritech.tnau.ac.in/about_us/abt_us.html \"About Us\") | [Success Stories](https://agritech.tnau.ac.in/success_stories/success_index.html \"Success Stories\") | [Farmers Association](https://agritech.tnau.ac.in/farm_association/farm_assoct.html \"Farmer's Association\") | [Farmers' Innovation](https://agritech.tnau.ac.in/farm_innovations/farm_innovations.html) | [Publications](https://agritech.tnau.ac.in/tnau_publish.html \"TNAU Publications\") | [Contact](https://agritech.tnau.ac.in/contact.html \"Contact Us\")  |   |  \n|  Post Harvest Diseases :: Fruits :: Mango  \n |  **Brown spot:_Pestalotia mangiferae_** **Symptoms:**\n  * The affected area of fruits becomes olivaceous-black and shrinks.\n  * Black dots appear at the centre of the spots represent the acervuli.\n  * On matured green fruits, small brown spots appear with greyish white centre which later turn to bigger lesions with large number of acervuli seen as black dots.\n\n  \n | ![](https://agritech.tnau.ac.in/crop_protection/images/posthar_mango/brownspot_2.jpg)  | ![](https://agritech.tnau.ac.in/crop_protection/images/posthar_mango/brownspot_1.jpg)  | ![](https://agritech.tnau.ac.in/crop_protection/images/posthar_mango/brownspot.jpg)  |  \n| --- | --- | --- |  \n| **Brown spot on leaves**  | **Black spots on twigs**  | **Black spots on fruits**  |  \n**Epidemiology:**\n  * Temp. between 20 and 250 C.\n  * Mycelial growth with sporulation takes place at pH 5.5 to 6.0.\n  * Wounding leads to more disease incidence.\n\n\nImage Source: <http://www.ivorychem.com/papers/MangoBrownSpotsManagementPaper.pdf>\n |  \n |  \n| \n* * *\n[Home](https://agritech.tnau.ac.in/index.html \"Home\") | [About Us](https://agritech.tnau.ac.in/about_us/abt_us.html \"About Us\") | [Success Stories](https://agritech.tnau.ac.in/success_stories/success_index.html \"Success Stories\") | [Farmers Association](https://agritech.tnau.ac.in/farm_association/farm_assoct.html \"Farmers Association\") | [Farmers' Innovation](https://agritech.tnau.ac.in/farm_innovations/farm_innovations.html) | [Publications](https://agritech.tnau.ac.in/tnau_publish.html \"TNAU Publications\") | [Contact Us ](https://agritech.tnau.ac.in/contact.html \"Contact Us\") © 2015 TNAU. All Rights Reserved.  |\n", "html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD XHTML 1.0 Transitional//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/xhtml1/DTD/xhtml1-transitional.dtd\"><html xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><head>\n<meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"keywords\" content=\"Agriculture, TNAU, Precision Farming, Organic Farming,Daily News Paper Farm Information, Daily Market Information, TNAU Weather,Horticulture, Organic Agriculture, Agriculture Engineering, Agriculture Marketing, Seed Certification, Crop Protection, Crop Insurance,Fishery, Forestry, Animal Husbandry, Sericulture, Commmunity Radio,KVK, E Extension Center,Govt Schemes &amp; Services,Variety Releases\">\n<title>TNAU Agritech Portal :: Crop Protection</title>\n<script type=\"text/javascript\">\n<!--\nfunction MM_openBrWindow(theURL,winName,features) { //v2.0\n  window.open(theURL,winName,features);\n}\n//-->\n</script>\n<style type=\"text/css\">\n<!--\nbody {\nmargin:0px auto;\n}\n.bord\n{\n\tborder-right:1px solid \n}\n.tit\n{\n\tcolor:#666666;\n\tfont-size:16px;\n\n\tline-height:1.4;\n\tfont-family:Georgia, \"Times New Roman\", Times, serif;\n}\n#apDiv1 {\n\tposition:absolute;\n\tleft:-1px;\n\ttop:-2px;\n\twidth:936px;\n\theight:1